<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian grain supply/disposal estimates.</title>
<headline>Australian grain supply/disposal estimates.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Bureau of Agricultural and Resource Economics (ABARE), Australia's official commodities forecasting agency, issued the following forecasts of the supply and disposal of Australian wheat, barley and sorghum grown in the 1997/98 season ending March 31, 1998.</p>
<p>Based on data as at July 2, in million tonnes:</p>
<p>				   1997/98    1996/97     1995/96</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p>    Production		  16.245     23.590     16.98</p>
<p>    Domestic use		 4.39	 3.51	 4.12</p>
<p>	Human and industrial   1.86	 1.85	 1.84</p>
<p>	Feed			 2.10	 1.18	 1.78</p>
<p>	Seed			 0.43	 0.49	 0.50</p>
<p>    Net Exports		 11.50	19.42	12.75</p>
<p>    Change in stocks	  +0.35	+0.66	+0.11</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>    Production		   4.15	 6.63	 5.82</p>
<p>    Domestic use		 2.77	 2.17	 1.98</p>
<p>     Malt, other human use   0.14	 0.13	 0.12</p>
<p>     Feed			  2.00	 1.90	 1.71</p>
<p>     Seed			  0.14	 0.14	 0.15</p>
<p>    Net Exports		  1.83	 4.86	 4.03</p>
<p>	Feed barley		2.60	 2.06	 1.69</p>
<p>	Malting barley	   1.05	 2.30	 1.89</p>
<p>	Malt (grain equiv)     0.52	 0.50	 0.46</p>
<p>SORGHUM</p>
<p>    Production		   1.42	 1.10	 1.56</p>
<p>    Domestic use		 1.05	 1.02	 0.95</p>
<p>Feed			 1.04	 1.01	 0.95</p>
<p>	Seed ('000 tonnes)	  3	    3	    2</p>
<p>Net exports ('000 tonnes)  372	  83	  603</p>
<p>(Any discrepancies are due to rounding)  </p>
<p>NOTE: Export estimates apply to marketing years of October-September for wheat, November-October for barley and March-February for sorghum.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
